Q: Limiting node.js&#39;s memory usage A: <p>There are two ways to increase the maximum memory size of V8:</p>
<ol>
<li>Using a <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/cli.html#--max-old-space-sizesize-in-megabytes" rel="nofollow noreferrer">CLI option</a>: <code>node --max-old-space-size=4096 memory.js</code></li>
<li>Using an <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/cli.html#node_optionsoptions" rel="nofollow noreferrer">env variable</a>: <code>NODE_OPTIONS='--max-old-space-size=4096' node memory.js</code></li>
</ol>
<p>Here's a small script that shows you the memory usage of your application:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const process = require('node:process');

const used = process.memoryUsage().heapUsed / 1024 / 1024;
console.log(`This app is currently using ${Math.floor(used)} MB of memory.`);
</code></pre>
